      "note": "Dimensions and outlines read off the side, plan and front views (tools/trace/b735/); the figures are the aircraft's measurements, not a copy of the drawing. The 737-300's points moved by the fuselage plugs, then snapped onto this sheet. Plain wing tips, as the sheet draws them. The sheet draws the cabin windows; the one behind the wing's line in the drawing is placed at its own position. The side view draws the fuselage 3.93 m tall (line centres) where the sheet prints 4.01 m and the front view draws 3.99 m, so the shape is fit to the printed height (fit_height.py). The side view draws the engine's inlet lip 8.94 m from the nose and the plan view 9.63 m; the sheet prints 9.35 m (the 737-300, -400 and -500 sheets all draw the plan's nacelle 0.69 m further back than the side's). The nacelle is moved 0.41 m back to the printed figure (build.py, as for any inlet more than 1.5% off); the wing stays where the plan draws it. Confidence medium for the views' disagreement."
    }
